 "notes": ["Quarters before Yahoo's 5-quarter window (the year-over-year base) and figures Yahoo's statements lack are from the company's SEC filings (XBRL company facts: 10-K / 10-Q); a fiscal Q4 is the 10-K year minus the 10-Q nine months, its diluted EPS Q4 net income / Q4 diluted shares, and EBIT / EBITDA pre-tax income + interest expense (+ depreciation & amortisation) when that matches Yahoo's own figures (computed ones are listed in \"derived\").", "Cash flow from the company's SEC filings (XBRL: operating cash flow NetCashProvidedByUsedInOperatingActivities, capex PaymentsToAcquirePropertyPlantAndEquipment, finance-lease principal FinanceLeasePrincipalPayments), drawn as the Capex tab's SEC cash-flow table: 10-Q cash-flow figures are year-to-date, so a quarter without its own 3-month figure is the difference of two (Q2 = H1 - Q1, Q4 = full year - 9 months). FCF = operating cash flow - capex; FCF after leases also subtracts the finance-lease principal payments. FCF QoQ / YoY only between two positive values.", "Q1 25: computed as the fiscal year minus its other three quarters where Yahoo's quarterly statements lack them; the fields are listed in \"derived\".", "Q4 25: diluted EPS from Yahoo's reported EPS where it matches net income / diluted shares, else net income / diluted shares (Yahoo's statements lack it).", "Fiscal labels are the company's own fiscal year, named by the calendar year it ends in.", "PER uses the trailing 4 quarters' diluted EPS (annual: the year's), ROA the trailing 4 quarters' net income over average total assets. The (E) EPS is the analysts' consensus, on Yahoo's EPS basis (\"EPS (Yahoo basis)\": for US companies usually adjusted, non-GAAP)."]
